+### RTERM advanced demo candidate
+
+`SAMPLES/rterm-advanced-7000.a` is a generated transient application, not a
+resident ASM feature. Its [operator guide](RTERM_ADVANCED_DEMO.md) records
+the source, memory layout, explicit RMP/1 handoff, and test commands.
+The focused `rterm-demo-check` gate builds it, checks byte-exact assembly
+with real ASM-F2 under py65, and exercises its protocol/application paths.
+It is a separate focused gate; it is not added to `asm-test`.
+
+Host evidence on 2026-09-16: 3,241 emitted bytes (2,523 high code/data and
+718 low data); CRC/escaping, session negotiation, acknowledgements,
+duplicate/damaged/oversize/stale frames, invalid AID/value rejection,
+fixed binary PUT, bounded receive timeout, GOODBYE, stack/zero-page restore,
+and writes confined to the declared RAM pass. The actual RTERM executable
+also passes a PTY run with field editing, local error/reset, F5 AID,
+CONTROL/TERMINAL/SCREEN/FILE/MESSAGE traffic, exact binary file completion,
+existing-file rejection, and exit.
+
+Physical-board acceptance is **pending**. Assemble and run on the current
+firmware, observe display/OIA and field behavior, verify the exact received
+file, repeat with an existing destination and no write root, exercise normal
+exit and disconnect/reconnect, then physically reset and verify ordinary raw
+monitor/ASM recovery. Append the resulting transcript under `LOGS`; host PTYs
+do not establish timing, physical flow control, or board recovery proof.
+
 ### HIMON/ASM ABI single-source gate
 
