+## 2026-09-16 BSO2 Installation In Bank 2
+
+At the user's request, the newest preserved BSO2 source was copied unchanged
+from `C:\SRC\bso2 backups\GitHub\bso2`, built with its original WDC commands,
+and combined with the exact required WDC service ROM at `$F800-$FFFF`.
+The complete 32 KB image was installed through STR8-N 1.34 on COM4 using
+`I / 2 / 8-F`, TYPE `FF`, description `BSO-2`. COMMIT returned `OK`.
+
+Complete flash archives were retained before and after installation.
+Independent readback matched all 32 KB of Bank 2, preserved Banks 0 and 1,
+and proved Bank 3 changed only in D2 enrollment. HIMON, ASM-F2, STR8-N, other
+directory rows, configuration, and vectors remain byte-exact.
+
+`J2` booted `basic system operations/2`, version `b s o / 2 v0 . 9`.
+Short/full help, ROM identity, RAM deposit/readback, disassembly, and hardware
+vector inspection passed. The board was left at the BSO2 `-` prompt; serial
+was closed. Physical RESET/power-cycle persistence was not separately tested.
+
+See the [installation record](BSO2_B2_INSTALL_2026-09-16.md) for source
+provenance, image hashes, backup locations, and checks. The append-only
+[raw transcript](BSO2_B2_INSTALL_2026-09-16.jsonl) is 3,918,156 bytes, SHA-256
+`d07b2bae0afbf862532a01295610f0e654f17d4496b7a1b05bcde3de47f00a5e`.
